    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d910">

                <pb facs="0857" n="847" xml:id="pg847"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/2456: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-04-08T16:00:00+09:00">April 8, 1941—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 8—3:07 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My April 8, 1 p.m. In view of the fact that Municipal Council has received a
                    letter from a terrorist organization threatening violence in connection with
                    reorganization of Settlement, the Chinese authorities at Chungking may wish to
                    consider making a public announcement of their acquiescence in reallocation of
                    seats or at least to inform Chinese Ratepayers Association at Shanghai of
                    acquiescence.</p>
                <p>Sent to Chungking, repeated to Department and Peiping, code text by air mail to
                    Tokyo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
